        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<div class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/1dd283e56ed97a6cd063f6eefa842991\"></div><p>What is the volume of the cube?</p>",
            "readable_text": "[IMG: /graphics/1dd283e56ed97a6cd063f6eefa842991]\n\nWhat is the volume of the cube?",
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "/graphics/1dd283e56ed97a6cd063f6eefa842991",
                "alt": ""
              }
            ],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The volume <span class=\"math\">[MATH: V]</span> of a cube can be found using the formula</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: V = s^3,]</span></p><p>where <span class=\"math\">[MATH: s]</span> is the side length of the cube.</p><p>Substituting <span class=\"math\">[MATH: s=4\\,\\textrm{cm}]</span> into the formula, we get \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: V = (4\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 64\\, \\textrm{cm}^3 .]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The volume [MATH: V] of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n[MATH: V = s^3,]\n\nwhere [MATH: s] is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting [MATH: s=4\\,\\textrm{cm}] into the formula, we get\n[MATH: V = (4\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 64\\, \\textrm{cm}^3 .]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [
          {
            "src": "/graphics/1dd283e56ed97a6cd063f6eefa842991",
            "alt": ""
          }
        ],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\n[IMG: /graphics/1dd283e56ed97a6cd063f6eefa842991]\n\nWhat is the volume of the cube?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nThe volume [MATH: V] of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n[MATH: V = s^3,]\n\nwhere [MATH: s] is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting [MATH: s=4\\,\\textrm{cm}] into the formula, we get\n[MATH: V = (4\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 64\\, \\textrm{cm}^3 .]"
      },
