          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we find the volume of a single container: </p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3}{6} = 8 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3]</span></p><p>Now, we need to find the side length of one container. </p><p>Since the volume of a cube is </p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: V = s^3,]</span></p><p>where <span class=\"math\">[MATH: s]</span> is the length of a side, we can find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: s]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: s = \\sqrt[3]{V} = \\sqrt[3]{8} = 2]</span></p><p>Therefore, the length of a side of a single container is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\,\\textrm{ft}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we find the volume of a single container:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3}{6} = 8 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3]\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of one container.\n\nSince the volume of a cube is\n\n[MATH: V = s^3,]\n\nwhere [MATH: s] is the length of a side, we can find [MATH: s] as follows:\n\n[MATH: s = \\sqrt[3]{V} = \\sqrt[3]{8} = 2]\n\nTherefore, the length of a side of a single container is [MATH: 2\\,\\textrm{ft}.]",
